  "title": "expert: Have coverity ignore allocation of expert modules",
  "description": "They're allocated in epan scope, which is always freed at program exit,\nso don't complain about how the storage isn't freed.\n\nIt's more difficult to do this for functions that take an allocator\nthat might possibly be NULL, especially as coverity can't figure out\nthat pinfo->pool won't be NULL.",
